{# The homepage shows the product instead of describing it: one sentence, then a small stage where three AIs take
   turns over one vault (assets/home-loop.js). Depth is one click away, never on this page: `npm run check` holds it
   to a word budget. #}
<main class="home">
    <section class="home-hero">
        <div class="say">
            <h1>One vault. <em>Any AI.</em></h1>
            <p class="lede">Tell Claude, ChatGPT or a local model something once. It lands in a vault you own, and any AI you connect can find it.</p>
            <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/use/start/">Start free on Parachute Cloud</a> <a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/run/self-host/">Or run your own</a></p>
            <ul class="ticks">
                <li>Open source</li>
                <li>Plain markdown you can take with you</li>
                <li>Free in the open beta</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        {# The stage. Without script it is the first scene's last frame: Claude has saved a note and a task (and the
           other two names, which would do nothing, aren't shown). #}
        <figure class="stage" data-vault="landed" aria-label="An example: three AIs take turns over one vault">
            <div class="ai">
                <div class="ai-bar">
                    <div class="ai-pick" role="group" aria-label="Which AI is talking">
                        <button type="button" aria-pressed="true">Claude</button>
                        <button type="button" aria-pressed="false">ChatGPT</button>
                        <button type="button" aria-pressed="false">Local model</button>
                    </div>
                    <button class="pause" type="button" aria-label="Pause" hidden><span></span></button>
                </div>
                <div class="chat">
                    <div class="scene">
                        <p class="you typed">Remember: the seed library box goes by the garden gate. Ask Maya if the garden will host it.</p>
                        <p class="it typed"><b class="who">Claude</b><span class="txt">Saved a note and a task, linked to Maya.</span></p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="chute" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#pchute"/></svg></div>
            <div class="vault">
                <p class="vault-head"><b>Your vault</b><span>the same one, whichever AI you use</span></p>
                <ul class="records">
                    <li class="rec"><i>Person</i><b>Maya</b><span>runs the garden</span></li>
                    <li class="rec"><i>Book</i><b>Piranesi</b><span>reading</span></li>
                    <li class="rec new note"><i>Note</i><b>Seed library box</b><span>goes by the garden gate</span></li>
                    <li class="rec new task"><i>Task</i><b>Ask Maya about hosting</b><span class="state"><span class="open">open</span><span class="done">done</span></span></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <figcaption>A drawing, with made-up notes. We've tested each AI on its own, Claude the most; the hand-off between them isn't a recorded run yet. <a href="/docs/use/connect-your-ai/">How far each AI is tested</a></figcaption>
        </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="home-ways" aria-labelledby="ways">
        <h2 id="ways">Two ways in</h2>
        <div class="way-grid">
            <a class="way" href="/docs/use/start/">
                <h3>Parachute Cloud</h3>
                <p>We run it. You get a vault in about a minute.</p>
                <span class="price">Free in the open beta</span>
                <span class="go">Start free</span>
            </a>
            <a class="way" href="/docs/run/self-host/">
                <h3>Your own machine</h3>
                <p>One command on a Mac or a Linux box.</p>
                <span class="price">Free, open source</span>
                <span class="go">Run your own</span>
            </a>
        </div>
        <p class="ways-note">A vault moves between them as a folder of plain markdown. There's a third way too: <a href="/docs/run/own-cloudflare/">your own Cloudflare</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-real">
        <details>
            <summary><span>See it for real</span> <small>three screens from claude.ai</small></summary>
            <div class="real-grid">
                <figure>
                    <img src="/assets/shots/claude-capture.webp" width="780" height="330" loading="lazy" alt="claude.ai: 'Jot this down in Parachute test: a seed library box at the garden gate…', and Claude's answer: two records added, a note and a task, linked to Maya">
                    <figcaption><b>It remembers.</b> Say it once; a note and a task are filed, linked to the people in them.</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                    <img src="/assets/shots/claude-live-board.webp" width="1100" height="509" loading="lazy" alt="claude.ai: asked for a live board of open tasks, Claude built one beside the chat, tasks grouped by project, each with a circle to tick">
                    <figcaption><b>Live pages.</b> Ask for a board; it reads your vault each time, and a tick writes back. <a href="/docs/use/claude-artifacts/">How</a></figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                    <img src="/assets/shots/claude-skill.webp" width="780" height="520" loading="lazy" alt="claude.ai: a product card for Fernhill Pottery's speckled oat mugs, in the shop's voice, signed 'Fired with care.'">
                    <figcaption><b>Your ways.</b> A skill in your vault says how you do something. <a href="/docs/use/skills/">How</a></figcaption>
